      "summaries": {
        "en": "Brave is an open-source web browser built on Chromium that prioritizes user privacy by blocking intrusive ads and trackers by default. Its technical innovation lies in integrating a privacy-first architecture directly into the browser core, rather than relying on add-ons, which reduces performance overhead and enhances security. Developers can use Brave as a testing environment for privacy-compliant web applications, examine its source code to learn about implementing privacy features in large-scale software, or contribute to its development on GitHub to help shape the future of private browsing.",
        "zh": "Brave是一款基于Chromium的开源网页浏览器，核心目标是解决网络隐私问题，通过默认屏蔽广告和追踪器来保护用户数据。其技术亮点在于将隐私保护架构深度集成到浏览器内核中，而非依赖插件，这种设计减少了性能损耗并提升了安全性。开发者可将Brave用作测试隐私友好型网页应用的环境，通过研究其源代码学习如何在大规模软件中实现隐私功能，或在GitHub上参与开发，共同推动隐私浏览技术的进步。",
        "es": "Brave is an open-source web browser built on Chromium that prioritizes user privacy by blocking intrusive ads and trackers by default. Its technical innovation lies in integrating a privacy-first architecture directly into the browser core, rather than relying on add-ons, which reduces performance overhead and enhances security. Developers can use Brave as a testing environment for privacy-compliant web applications, examine its source code to learn about implementing privacy features in large-scale software, or contribute to its development on GitHub to help shape the future of private browsing.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "brave-browser stands out for brave, browser, and chromium in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "Brave is an open-source web browser built on Chromium that prioritizes user privacy by blocking intrusive ads and trackers by default. Its technical innovation lies in integrating a privacy-first architecture directly into the browser core, rather than relying on add-ons, which reduces performance overhead and enhances security. Developers can use Brave as a testing environment for privacy-compliant web applications, examine its source code to learn about implementing privacy features in large-scale software, or contribute to its development on GitHub to help shape the future of private browsing.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/brave/brave-browser for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
