      "summaries": {
        "en": "gogcli is a command-line interface tool that simplifies accessing and managing Google Suite services like Gmail, Calendar, Drive, and Contacts directly from the terminal. Its technical strength lies in using Go's efficient concurrency model to handle multiple API requests simultaneously, making batch operations faster than traditional web interfaces. Developers can use it to automate routine tasks—such as backing up emails or syncing calendar events—by writing simple scripts, and can extend its functionality by adding new Google API integrations through its modular design.",
        "zh": "gogcli 是一个命令行工具，让开发者能通过终端直接访问和管理 Gmail、日历、云盘及联系人等 Google 套件服务。它采用 Go 语言的高效并发模型，可同时处理多个 API 请求，使批量操作比传统网页界面更快。用户可通过编写脚本自动化日常任务，例如备份邮件或同步日程，还能基于其模块化设计轻松集成新的 Google API 来扩展功能，适合需要高效管理云端数据的开发者和团队。",
        "es": "gogcli is a command-line interface tool that simplifies accessing and managing Google Suite services like Gmail, Calendar, Drive, and Contacts directly from the terminal. Its technical strength lies in using Go's efficient concurrency model to handle multiple API requests simultaneously, making batch operations faster than traditional web interfaces. Developers can use it to automate routine tasks—such as backing up emails or syncing calendar events—by writing simple scripts, and can extend its functionality by adding new Google API integrations through its modular design.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "gogcli stands out for gcal, gcontacts, and gdrive in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "gogcli is a command-line interface tool that simplifies accessing and managing Google Suite services like Gmail, Calendar, Drive, and Contacts directly from the terminal. Its technical strength lies in using Go's efficient concurrency model to handle multiple API requests simultaneously, making batch operations faster than traditional web interfaces. Developers can use it to automate routine tasks—such as backing up emails or syncing calendar events—by writing simple scripts, and can extend its functionality by adding new Google API integrations through its modular design.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/steipete/gogcli for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
